# F-2 (docs/lote-3/seguridad-2026-09-14.md, Alto). This directory is
# reachable straight from the web through the public/storage symlink
# (`artisan storage:link`, documented in docs/lote-2/README.md) — it is NOT
# behind Laravel's router. Today the ONLY thing stopping a PHP file from
# landing here and being executed is App\Filament\Support\SecureImageUpload's
# MIME whitelist at the application layer (see its docblock and F-2 part B
# of the audit): one future `->image()` field, one disk misconfiguration
# (see F-4 / config/livewire.php), or one bug in that single check, and this
# becomes remote code execution. This file removes the OTHER half of the
# chain — server-side execution — so a file that slips past validation is
# still just a static file, never a script, no matter how it got here.
#
# Applies to this directory AND its subdirectories (destinations/,
# experiences/, team/, tours/, etc.) unless AllowOverride on the vhost
# blocks .htaccess inheritance — see the deploy-day check in
# docs/lote-2/README.md.
#
# Belt-and-suspenders, three independent mechanisms, because a single one
# can be absent or disabled on a given host:

# 1) Turn the PHP engine off for this directory outright (classic mod_php).
<IfModule mod_php.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_php7.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_php8.c>
    php_flag engine off
</IfModule>

# 2) Deny access outright to anything with an executable-looking extension,
#    regardless of which handler would have run it (mod_php, PHP-FPM/
#    FastCGI via mod_fcgid/mod_proxy_fcgi, CGI). Also denies .html/.htm/.svg:
#    the upload whitelist only ever writes .jpg/.png/.webp here (see
#    SecureImageUpload::configure()), so a request for anything else in this
#    tree is never legitimate traffic.
<FilesMatch "\.(php|phtml|pht|phar|php[3-8]?|phps|cgi|fcgi|pl|py|asp|aspx|sh|jsp|htaccess|htm|html|svg)$">
    <IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
        Require all denied
    </IfModule>
    <IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
        Order allow,deny
        Deny from all
    </IfModule>
</FilesMatch>

# 3) Strip any handler/MIME mapping that would make Apache execute these
#    extensions as PHP instead of serving them as plain files (defence in
#    depth in case rule 2 above is ever bypassed, e.g. by a proxy that
#    doesn't honour <FilesMatch>).
<IfModule mod_mime.c>
    RemoveHandler .php .phtml .pht .phar .php3 .php4 .php5 .php6 .php7 .php8 .phps .cgi .fcgi .pl .py
    RemoveType .php .phtml .pht .phar .php3 .php4 .php5 .php6 .php7 .php8 .phps
</IfModule>

# LiteSpeed reads Apache-style .htaccess (its docs claim broad
# compatibility with mod_rewrite/mod_authz_core directives), but this was
# NOT verified against a real LiteSpeed instance -- there is no server yet.
# Re-verify all three mechanisms above the day there is one; see the
# checklist in docs/lote-2/README.md.
